  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1237 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nHot conditions are expected throughout the forecast with highs \nin the upper 90s to low 100s each day and upper 60s to upper \n70s each night. There will be a persistent trough of low \npressure across portions of western Kansas throughout the \nforecast in which a few thunderstorms may form along during peak\nheating. Otherwise expect dry conditions with winds from a \nsoutherly direction. Apparent temperatures look to reach towards\n105 degrees in the afternoon over the next few days and a heat \nadvisory may be needed in the future. In addition, low RHs and \nbreezy conditions look to elevate fire weather risk through the \nbeginning of next week.",
